Resultant force in x-direction, [latex]\begin{aligned}
    R_{x}&=P\cos 60^{\circ}-Q\sin 15^{\circ}-R\sin 15^{\circ} \\  &=100\cos 60^{\circ}-250\sin 15^{\circ}-150\sin 15^{\circ} \\  &=-159.59\, kN\left ( \rightarrow \right ) \\  &=-159.59\, kN\left ( \rightarrow \right ) \\  &=159.59\, kN\left ( \leftarrow \right )
\end{aligned}[/latex] Resultant force in y-direction, [latex]\begin{aligned}
    R_{y}&=P\sin 60^{\circ}+Q\cos 15^{\circ}-R\sin 15^{\circ} \\  &=100\sin 60^{\circ}+250\cos 15^{\circ}-150\sin 15^{\circ} \\  &=289.26\, kN \left ( \uparrow \right )
\end{aligned}[/latex] Final resultant force, [latex]\begin{aligned}
    R&=\sqrt{R^{2}_{x}+R^{2}_{y}}=330.4\, kN \\ \theta &=\tan ^{-1}\left ( \frac{159.59}{289.56} \right ) \\ \theta &=28.9^{\circ}
\end{aligned}[/latex] Direction with respect to x-axis [latex]\begin{aligned}
    &=\theta+90^{\circ} \\  &=28.9^{\circ}+90^{\circ} \\  &=118.9^{\circ}
\end{aligned}[/latex]

