Total float can be determined once the activity times i.e. EST, EFT, LST and LFT are known. total float,[latex]\begin{aligned}
F_{T}&=LST-EST\\ &=LFT-EFT
\end{aligned}[/latex] For activity 5-7, [latex]\begin{aligned}
 EST&=38\\ EFT&=63\\ LFT&=63\\ LST&=38\\ F_{T}&=0
\end{aligned}[/latex] for activity 11-12, [latex]\begin{aligned}
 EST&=80\\ EFT&=81\\ LFT&=81 \\ LST&=80 \\ F_T&=0
\end{aligned}[/latex] [latex]\textbf{Note}[/latex]:It can be seen directly that since the slack of all events are zero, there is not margin left for the occurence of events and therefore. Maximum available line=Time required for completion of activity [latex]\therefore \; F_{t}[/latex] for all activities is zero.

